POST /v1/learners
Request: {displayName, dateOfBirth, avatarId?, idempotencyKey}
Reject additional fields with a strict schema.
Response: {learner:{id,displayName,dateOfBirth,ageYears,ageMonths,ageAsOfDate,avatarId,version}, onboardingStatus}

GET /v1/learners
Return only learners owned by or explicitly shared with the authenticated parent. For LP-001, ownership is the implemented path.

GET /v1/learner-context/{learnerId}
For authorized platform/app launch services, return {learnerId,displayName,avatarId,ageYears,ageMonths,ageAsOfDate,locale,timezone}. Raw dateOfBirth is excluded by default.

All endpoints first enforce parent account status. Soft-deleted parents receive ACCOUNT_DELETED with no learner payload.

GET /v1/learners/{learnerId}
Return the full parent-authorized editable learner read model: id, displayName, dateOfBirth, ageYears, ageMonths, ageAsOfDate, avatarId, version, createdAt, updatedAt.

PATCH /v1/learners/{learnerId}
Strict request: {displayName?, dateOfBirth?, avatarId?, expectedVersion, idempotencyKey}. avatarId:null removes avatar. Require at least one editable field. Reject learnerId, ownerParentId, householdId, status, subscription, entitlement, progress, mastery and all unknown fields.
Response: {learner:{id,displayName,dateOfBirth,ageYears,ageMonths,ageAsOfDate,avatarId,version,updatedAt}, changedFields, noOp}.
All endpoints check parent account status and ownership before returning learner data.
